<title>POLAND: POLISH BUDGET DEFICIT UP TO PLN 6.41 BLN IN OCT.</title>
<headline>POLISH BUDGET DEFICIT UP TO PLN 6.41 BLN IN OCT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish budget deficit widened</p>
<p>by 260 million to 6.41 billion zlotys in October, which</p>
<p>accounted for 63.1 percent of the planned 1996 deficit of 10.16</p>
<p>billion zlotys, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p> POLISH BUDGET GAP   Jan-October     Jan-September 1996 plan</p>
<p> balance in bln PLN	-6.41	     -6.15	-10.16</p>
<p> revenue		     79.86	     70.02	100.17</p>
<p> expenditure		 86.28	     76.17	110.33</p>
<p>NOTE: Jan-September figures given as reported last month.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
